  "code": "1556",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"79\" data-end=\"144\">\n<p data-start=\"81\" data-end=\"144\"><strong data-start=\"81\" data-end=\"94\">Protein S</strong> is a <strong data-start=\"100\" data-end=\"143\">vitamin K&ndash;dependent plasma glycoprotein</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"145\" data-end=\"291\">\n<p data-start=\"147\" data-end=\"291\">It functions as a <strong data-start=\"165\" data-end=\"200\">cofactor to activated Protein C</strong>, helping degrade <strong data-start=\"218\" data-end=\"251\">clotting factors Va and VIIIa</strong>, thus preventing excess clot formation.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"292\" data-end=\"458\">\n<p data-start=\"294\" data-end=\"324\">Exists in two forms in plasma:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"327\" data-end=\"458\">\n<li data-start=\"327\" data-end=\"381\">\n<p data-start=\"329\" data-end=\"381\"><strong data-start=\"329\" data-end=\"347\">Free Protein S</strong> (functionally active) &ndash; about 40%</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"384\" data-end=\"458\">\n<p data-start=\"386\" data-end=\"458\"><strong data-start=\"386\" data-end=\"405\">Bound Protein S</strong> (inactive, bound to C4b-binding protein) &ndash; about 60%</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Free Protein S Level</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Clinical Significance</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Normal</strong></td>\n<td>Adequate anticoagulant activity. No concern for Protein S deficiency.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Low (&lt;60%)</strong></td>\n<td>Suggests <strong>Protein S deficiency</strong>, may be hereditary or acquired.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Very low</strong></td>\n<td>Higher risk for <strong>venous thromboembolism (VTE)</strong> or <strong>recurrent miscarriages</strong>.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"1476\" data-end=\"1513\"><strong data-start=\"1480\" data-end=\"1513\">Causes of Low Free Protein S:</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"1515\" data-end=\"1558\"><strong data-start=\"1520\" data-end=\"1558\">1. Inherited Protein S Deficiency:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1559\" data-end=\"1769\">\n<li data-start=\"1559\" data-end=\"1628\">\n<p data-start=\"1561\" data-end=\"1628\"><strong data-start=\"1561\" data-end=\"1571\">Type I</strong>: Decreased total and free Protein S + decreased activity</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1629\" data-end=\"1701\">\n<p data-start=\"1631\" data-end=\"1701\"><strong data-start=\"1631\" data-end=\"1642\">Type II</strong>: Normal level, but decreased function (qualitative defect)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1702\" data-end=\"1769\">\n<p data-start=\"1704\" data-end=\"1769\"><strong data-start=\"1704\" data-end=\"1716\">Type III</strong>: Normal total, decreased free Protein S and activity</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1771\" data-end=\"1799\"><strong data-start=\"1776\" data-end=\"1799\">2. Acquired Causes:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1800\" data-end=\"2054\">\n<li data-start=\"1800\" data-end=\"1826\">\n<p data-start=\"1802\" data-end=\"1826\"><strong data-start=\"1802\" data-end=\"1826\">Vitamin K deficiency</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1827\" data-end=\"1846\">\n<p data-start=\"1829\" data-end=\"1846\"><strong data-start=\"1829\" data-end=\"1846\">Liver disease</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1847\" data-end=\"1869\">\n<p data-start=\"1849\" data-end=\"1869\"><strong data-start=\"1849\" data-end=\"1869\">Warfarin therapy</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1870\" data-end=\"1885\">\n<p data-start=\"1872\" data-end=\"1885\"><strong data-start=\"1872\" data-end=\"1885\">Pregnancy</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1886\" data-end=\"1934\">\n<p data-start=\"1888\" data-end=\"1934\"><strong data-start=\"1888\" data-end=\"1934\">Oral contraceptive use or estrogen therapy</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1935\" data-end=\"1985\">\n<p data-start=\"1937\" data-end=\"1985\"><strong data-start=\"1937\" data-end=\"1985\">Disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1986\" data-end=\"2022\">\n<p data-start=\"1988\" data-end=\"2022\"><strong data-start=\"1988\" data-end=\"2022\">Acute thrombosis (consumption)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2023\" data-end=\"2054\">\n<p data-start=\"2025\" data-end=\"2054\"><strong data-start=\"2025\" data-end=\"2054\">HIV or nephrotic syndrome</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
